Security fixes for PHP 5.2.17 from the PHP-5.2-security-backports branch of
https://github.com/shivammathur/php-src-backports (up to ff60deb117a7, which
includes the CVE-2026-109618/CVE-2026-109619 backport), minus what
php52-backports and PLD patches already carry, adapted to that tree.

Ported from php-src on top of that:
- 3655b79c7bfa CVE-2026-91765 (GHSA-rgrp-mwpx-f6rm) SOAP unbounded recursion
- 5af9465ca890, 795440a704d4 CVE-2026-91766 (GHSA-fpwc-w8rq-cr92) credentials
  sent to another origin on redirect
- 547566f17a12, 64664758cd8e CVE-2026-93682 (GHSA-7875-c8px-7q5f) empty Location
- 41d49abbd99d CVE-2025-1736 (GHSA-hgf5-96fm-v528) user header detection
- b4e3397ec8f4 CVE-2026-92842 (GHSA-88hq-2827-7pg6) convert.* lbchars with NUL
- b11bd1d9390b CVE-2025-14181 (GHSA-cj93-vc83-wgqv) SOAP HTTP body size overflow
- 7ac9700d0d46 GHSA-ch8v-r6jh-4vvr FILTER_SANITIZE_ENCODED and 0xFF
- c5f28c7cf0a0 CVE-2025-14177 (GHSA-3237-qqm7-mfv7) getimagesize APPn short read
- 9164dc11e232, 0e715e71d945 GHSA-wg4p-4hqh-c3g9 XML_OPTION_SKIP_TAGSTART
- ed70b1ea43a9 GHSA-www2-q4fc-65wf NUL bytes in dns/inet/getserv* arguments
- 66bd809ac922 CVE-2025-1735 (GHSA-hrwm-9436-5mv3) pgsql escaping errors
- a38418777f65 CVE-2026-7258 (GHSA-m8rr-4c36-8gq4) urldecode isxdigit()
- metaphone(): int overflow of the 5.2 phoneme buffer (CVE-2026-7568 area)
- b061fa909de7 CVE-2016-10397 (bug #73192) parse_url() host confusion
- 4a89e726bd4d parse_url() userinfo parsing restored, as upstream did after
  the #77423 fix; FILTER_VALIDATE_URL keeps the userinfo check
- aee3b3ac9b81 CVE-2026-6722 (GHSA-85c2-q967-79q5): the SOAP ref_map references
  are released after decoding, as upstream does
- 3584a98bda0f GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w: post_max_size enforced for multipart bodies
  without a Content-Length (the session upload progress part has no 5.2
  counterpart)
Generated re2c scanners are not part of this patch; the spec regenerates them
from the patched .re files. Regression tests live in the branch above.

